BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 663.32 Tm (Section 3: Where Practitioners Disagree & Alternative Playbooks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 641.10 Tm (The lien camp splits on whether a recorded judgment is a weapon or a waiting room. Will at Downs Law) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 625.87 Tm (treats the Georgia fifa recorded with the superior court as one of three core methods, but concedes up front) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 610.65 Tm (that it 'doesn't necessarily get you paid right then'. The payoff only lands when the debtor tries to sell or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 595.42 Tm (refinance the house, lot, or investment property [K1KakWduA04 @ 00:00:43]. LawShelf pushes that warning) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 580.20 Tm (further: a judgment lien blocks a sale yet cannot force a foreclosure, it may sit for 20 years without producing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 564.97 Tm (a dollar, it has to be renewed, and interest keeps accruing the whole time [fQZc8moX-c4 @ 00:03:01]. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 549.75 Tm (National Law Review panel runs the lien as an active pressure lever instead of a parking spot. Jeff Leon) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 534.52 Tm (stacks liens with depositions, subpoenas, freezes, and credit-report hits to become a nuisance, noting that a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 519.30 Tm (lien can trip a default on the debtor's mortgage [R3nWxu374QE @ 00:19:30]. Tim Anenberger adds a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 504.07 Tm (priority angle the passive camp never touches: when property is held as tenancy by the entirety, record in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 488.85 Tm (chancery court immediately, because it is 'first in time, first in right' [R3nWxu374QE @ 00:16:35]. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 473.62 Tm (operator read: record fast for priority, but never count the lien as cash.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 458.40 Tm (Wage garnishment draws the sharpest split between the first-strike camp and the skeptics. Tim Anenberger) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 443.17 Tm (calls it the first tool in Mississippi. It creates a lien on the income stream, and when the debtor changes jobs) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 427.95 Tm (you simply re-issue it, though North Carolina bars it outright except for child support and taxes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 412.72 Tm ([R3nWxu374QE @ 00:12:48]. The Sterling Firm lays out its version as a low-cost grind: a $30 deposit, after) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 397.50 Tm (which the employer remits 25% of net wages starting 10 days after service, for up to 10 years) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 382.27 Tm ([UV-WyQ1-NC4 @ 00:04:15]. LawShelf undercuts the strategy for a big slice of debtors. The CCPA Title III) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 367.05 Tm (cap limits the take to the lesser of 25% of disposable earnings or earnings above 30 times the federal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 351.82 Tm (minimum wage, and garnishment simply fails on low income or unemployment [fQZc8moX-c4 @ 00:02:41].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 336.60 Tm (Private Investigator Videos goes further and calls wages slow, pushing operators toward leverage plays) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 321.37 Tm (instead: seize the debtor's business websites, email, and phone numbers so the business itself feels the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 306.15 Tm (squeeze [q-khGCaOPck @ 00:07:25]. The playbook choice comes down to the debtor profile. Steady) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 290.92 Tm (salaried earners get the wage order. Self-employed operators with digital storefronts get hit where the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 275.70 Tm (revenue actually flows.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 260.47 Tm (The practitioners also disagree on who should do the collecting and how hard to chase. Hendershot Cowart) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 245.25 Tm (P.C. ranks a Texas receiver as the 'last resort' because receivers 'typically take 25% of whatever is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 230.02 Tm (collected,' and the firm pitches its own work as running without that cut [-kyDpaMUqFY @ 00:01:44].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 214.80 Tm (Attorney Michael Ehline lists collection agencies as a normal California step alongside wage garnishment,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 199.57 Tm (liens, and renewing the judgment, treating the agency as just another tool in the kit [jPO9_I_LBSw @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 184.35 Tm (00:00:28]. Private Investigator Videos rejects that framing hard. Agencies are contingency phone-callers,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 169.12 Tm (giving away 'a third' may be permanent, and passive 'collection' is a different business from active 'recovery') Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 153.90 Tm ([q-khGCaOPck @ 00:11:17]. On how far to push, Jeff Leon argues for compromise priced on the time value) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 138.67 Tm (of money and risk, warning that clients who chase a judgment 'to the end of the earth' end up running 'two) Tj ET
