BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 381.05 Tm (that contact continuing after a 'stop' reply is actionable. The operating consensus is simple: every channel) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.82 Tm (restriction becomes enforceable the moment the consumer puts it on the record, and every post-notice) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 350.60 Tm (contact becomes a countable, documentable violation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 335.37 Tm (The third consensus pillar is the paper trail and the money behind it. Jansen describes the 5-in-5 rule: a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 320.15 Tm (validation notice within five days, with a tear-off dispute sheet, the original creditor, account number, and an) Tj ET
