BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 580.20 Tm (five accounts can absorb up to 35 calls in a week [9RtU4rpS3pw @ 00:05:51]. Night Ferry reads the same) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 564.97 Tm (rule as a presumption of violation rather than a hard cap, and notes that texts and emails are not counted) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 549.75 Tm (toward it, though each must still offer a simple opt-out [7HVra7o-cZg @ 00:03:24]. Jeff Loman of Guardian) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 534.52 Tm (Litigation Group pushes the frequency fight further, citing case law where 18 calls in a single day were not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 519.30 Tm (treated as harassing unless the collector actually spoke with the consumer [n3SZjPQDSHc @ 00:08:09].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 504.07 Tm (Michael Stillman, past president of the NCBA, attacks the rule from the collection-bar side: after a right-party) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 488.85 Tm (contact, no further contact is allowed within seven days without consent, which collides head-on with judges) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 473.62 Tm (who order a hallway call, prompting the attorney to ask the bench, "are you also going to indemnify me") Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 458.40 Tm ([9VNthZZ6JNk @ 00:08:37].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 443.17 Tm (Practitioners also split on how dangerous a single payment is on old paper. Jansen tells SeniorLiving.Org) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 427.95 Tm (viewers that a payment resets the statute of limitations in "almost every state," naming Texas as the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 412.72 Tm (exception, and pairs that with the ban on threatening suit over time-barred debt [9RtU4rpS3pw @ 00:17:58].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 397.50 Tm (WealthCurve opens with a narrower warning that paying can restart the clock only "in some states," puts) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 382.27 Tm (typical limitation periods at three to six years, and points to a 2023 CFPB advisory barring suit threats on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 367.05 Tm (time-barred debt [cKYmFnf_o2Q @ 00:04:42]. Loman widens the trigger list beyond money: a payment, a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 351.82 Tm (payment plan, or even an admission can reset the clock, and the statute only limits lawsuits, so collection) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 336.60 Tm (can continue "forever" while credit reporting runs seven years [n3SZjPQDSHc @ 00:29:22]. Brian Parker of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 321.37 Tm (KillDebt takes the most aggressive posture on threatened suits under section 1692e5, telling consumers to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 306.15 Tm ("wait it out" when a collector threatens litigation, and stressing that nobody can be garnished without a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 290.92 Tm (judgment [YYdsx06msa0 @ 00:07:04]. The playbook choice is stark: Jansen and Loman treat any) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 275.70 Tm (engagement on stale debt as a reset risk, while Parker treats an empty threat of suit as a strict-liability) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 260.47 Tm (violation in its own right.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 245.25 Tm (The paperwork camp splits hardest on how much to demand from a collector. Meet Jermaine, drawing on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 230.02 Tm (time spent working in debt collections, hands out a free four-letter bundle covering pay to delete, goodwill,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 214.80 Tm (cease and desist, and debt validation [XSfDS_s1URg @ 00:00:19]. Loman flatly rejects the 28-item) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 199.57 Tm (validation demands circulating online: "That is absolutely not the law," explaining that only three items are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 184.35 Tm (required, and warning that a written pay-for-delete can get an attorney classed as a credit repair) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 169.12 Tm (organization, so the safer route is getting deletion by email or informally [n3SZjPQDSHc @ 00:34:56].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 153.90 Tm (Attorney Aaron Swift runs a third playbook, sending third-party collectors a letter by fax or email that is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 138.67 Tm (explicitly not a validation letter, because validation only matters inside the first 30 days; it is built on Reg F,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 123.45 Tm (restricts contact channels and times such as 5:00 to 8:00 p.m., and disputes the debt [owpVxkqEbEk @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 108.22 Tm (00:03:29]. Jermaine insists every letter go by certified mail for a 16-digit tracking number, because with) Tj ET
